==English==

===Etymology===
From the former instruction on letters ‘haste, post, haste’, later reinterpreted as a compound of {{term|post}} + {{term|haste}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˌpəʊstˈheɪst/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌpoʊstˈheɪst/}}
* {{audio|en-us-posthaste.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[quickly]], as fast as someone travelling post; with great [[speed]]
#: ''It is imperative that you finish your task '''posthaste'''.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|quickly}} [[ASAP]], [[quickly]]
* See also [[Wikisaurus:quickly]]

====Quotations====
*'''1946''' — [[w:Paramahansa Yogananda|Paramahansa Yogananda]], ''[[s:Autobiography of a Yogi|Autobiography of a Yogi]]'', Ch. 17
*:"Sasi cannot last through the night." These words from his physician, and the spectacle of my friend, now reduced almost to a skeleton, sent me '''posthaste''' to Serampore.

